# Cloudflare Pages response headers (served from the deployed site root).
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. `npm run build` runs scripts/csp-postbuild.mjs after
# `astro build`, which replaces the two placeholders below in dist/_headers:
#   __CSP_SCRIPT_HASHES__  SHA-256 hashes of every inline <script> Starlight
#                          emits (theme provider, sidebar state, search shortcut)
#   __CSP_STYLE_HASHES__   SHA-256 hashes of any inline <style> (normally none;
#                          astro.config sets build.inlineStylesheets: 'never')
# so script-src and style-src never need 'unsafe-inline'.
#
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is required by Pagefind (Starlight search), which compiles
# a WebAssembly module; it does not permit JavaScript eval().
#
# style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline' is the one residual: Expressive Code and
# Starlight render thousands of inline `style="--0:…"` attributes, whose hashes
# do not fit Cloudflare's 2,000-character limit for a _headers line. The
# post-build step therefore adds a per-page <meta http-equiv=CSP> with
# `style-src-attr 'unsafe-hashes' <hashes>`; browsers enforce both policies, so
# the effective policy allows only the exact attribute values on that page.
# See docs/deploy.md ("Content-Security-Policy") before changing anything here,
# and verify every CSP change against a Cloudflare Pages preview deploy.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' __CSP_SCRIPT_HASHES__; style-src 'self' __CSP_STYLE_HASHES__; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'
